### Why is work lost on shutdown?

The default commonPool uses daemon threads. When all non-daemon threads finish, the JVM exits and daemon threads are killed instantly.

```java
public static void main(String[] args) {
    CompletableFuture.runAsync(() -> {
        settleTrade("TRD-001"); // takes 5 seconds
    });
    // main() returns. No non-daemon threads left.
    // JVM exits. settleTrade killed mid-execution. LOST!
}
```

### How do you fix it with a non-daemon pool?

```java
ThreadPoolExecutor pool = new ThreadPoolExecutor(
    10, 20, 60, TimeUnit.SECONDS,
    new LinkedBlockingQueue<>(1000),
    r -> { Thread t = new Thread(r); t.setDaemon(false); return t; }
);

Runtime.getRuntime().addShutdownHook(new Thread(() -> {
    pool.shutdown();
    try { pool.awaitTermination(30, TimeUnit.SECONDS); }
    catch (InterruptedException e) { pool.shutdownNow(); }
}));

CompletableFuture.runAsync(() -> settleTrade("TRD-001"), pool);
```

